cation, glass and metal architectural elements, wood and steel furniture -> /services", "On-site installation services (assembly, welding, structural and decorative metal installation, public art placement) -> /services", "Public and private commissions for high-end residential, commercial, urban and public art -> /services", "Collaborations with architects, designers, and urban planners -> /about", "Materials: steel, honed concrete, glass, wood -> /about, /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Tutto Ferro is a Reno-based fabrication shop that prides itself on a foundation of quality, craftsmanship, and innovation.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tutto-ferro' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Twin City Sheet Metal operates from Brewer, Maine, where it was founded in 1951. The company runs a custom sheet metal and steel fabrication shop serving customers across the state.

The shop provides sheet metal fabrication, HVAC ductwork (pre‑fabricated and made‑to‑order), laser cutting, CNC bending and forming, and 3D modeling for design optimization. It works with steel, stainless steel, aluminum, and galvanized steel in thicknesses from 0.021 to 0.25 inches. Equipment includes a Cincinnati CNC 5‑axis press brake with Wilson Tooling, a programmable coil line, a spiral machine, and a nitrogen laser cutter capable of 59″ × 119″ parts. The company handles low‑volume prototypes through high‑volume production runs.

Customers span commercial, industrial, residential, and institutional sectors. Typical projects include ductwork for heating, cooling, and environmental control systems, as well as custom metal parts for a variety of applications. The firm works from initial design through fabrication and installation.

Twin City Sheet Metal emphasizes superior craftsmanship, rapid turnaround, and cost‑effective solutions backed by close customer collaboration. It differentiates itself through exclusive use of Wilson Tooling, a Cincinnati CNC press brake that adjusts after every bend, and in‑house coil line and spiral machinery for duct fabrication.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet metal fabrication", "HVAC ductwork fabrication", "Laser cutting", "CNC bending & forming", "CNC press brake forming", "Wilson Tooling", "3D modeling & engineering", "Welding", "Notching", "Shearing", "Rolling", "Plasma cutting", "Product design", "Installation", "Prototyping", "High-volume production"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial", "Residential", "Institutional"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Galvanized steel"], "equipment": ["Cincinnati CNC 5-axis press brake", "Wilson Tooling", "Programmable coil line", "Spiral machine", "Nitrogen laser cutter (59\" x 119\")"], "volume": "Low volume prototypes to high volume production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 75 years of experience (since 1951)", "Rapid turnaround times on prototypes and production runs", "Exclusive use of Wilson Tooling for consistent bending quality", "Cincinnati CNC 5\u2011axis press brake with automatic bend correction", "In\u2011house programmable coil line and spiral machine for ductwork"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1951 -> db", "Headquarters Brewer, Maine -> db", "Custom sheet metal and steel fabrication shop -> /", "Services: HVAC ductwork, laser cutting, bending/forming, 3D modeling -> /", "Materials: steel, stainless steel, aluminum, galvanized steel (0.021\u20130.25 in) -> /", "Equipment: Cincinnati CNC 5-axis press brake, Wilson Tooling, programmable coil line, spiral machine, nitrogen laser cutter (59x119) -> /", "Volume: low-volume prototypes to high-volume production runs -> /", "Industries: commercial, industrial, residential, i