UPDATE companies SET description='UEC Advanced Electronics operates from a 64,000-square-foot campus in Hanahan, South Carolina, within the Charleston region. The company was founded in 1995 as UEC Electronics, LLC (Ufkes Engineering and Consulting) by engineers Rebecca and Phil Ufkes, initially developing automation solutions for U.S. government vehicles and power-related products. Recognized as a small, woman-owned business in South Carolina, it became a subsidiary of Albion River LLC in 2025 after a series of acquisitions including Arotech Corporation (2014) and Greenbriar Equity Group (2019).

The company provides end-to-end product design and manufacturing for power storage, generation, and distribution systems. Its capabilities span engineering design, rapid prototyping, precision manufacturing, higher-level assembly, cable and harness assemblies, electromechanical assemblies, circuit card assemblies, and fully integrated multi-rack systems. Core products include mobile power distribution and management systems (MPDMS), modular high-voltage battery packs, intelligent battery systems, vehicle power systems, clean energy generation solutions, and power distribution units. The campus houses engineering, integration, production, and testing operations under one roof.

UEC serves mission-critical markets across defense, aerospace, medical, and industrial sectors. Its battery systems are engineered for aerospace, military, automotive, and renewable energy applications, while the MPDMS platform supports military operations and event management. The company also supports U.S. government vehicle programs and has participated in a Department of Defense mentoring program with Raytheon.

UEC differentiates itself through a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, and AS9100D, with ITAR registration and RoHS-compliant production lines. Its vision targets global leadership in mission-critical manufacturing, emphasizing agility, quality, technological excellence, and cost efficiency, backed by comprehensive testing, traceability, and continuous improvement.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','AS9100D','Underwriters Laboratories (UL)','Canadian Standards Association (CSA)','IPC-A-610 Class 1','IPC-A-610 Class 2','IPC-A-610 Class 3','IPC-J-STD-001','IPC-7711/21','MIL-STD-810','MIL-STD-202','AS5553D','ANSI/ESD S20.20-2021','ITAR-Registered','RoHS-compliant production lines']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering Design & Development", "Electronic Manufacturing Services", "Automation and Test", "Program Management", "Supply Chain Management", "Quality Services", "Concept Development", "Prototyping", "Detailed Design", "Testing and Validation", "Higher-Level Assembly", "Cable & Harness Assembly", "Electromechanical Assembly", "Precision Manufacturing", "Custom Manufacturing Solutions", "Mobile Power Distribution & Management Systems (MPDMS)", "Battery Systems Design & Manufacturing", "Power Distribution Systems", "Power Generation Systems", "Soldier Power Systems", "Vehicle Power Systems", "Clean Energy Generation Solutions", "Modular High-Voltage Battery Packs", "Circuit Card Assembly"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Medical", "Industrial", "Automotive", "Renewable Energy", "Event Management"], "materials": ["Lithium-ion", "Advanced battery chemistries"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end product design and manufacturing under one roof", "64,000+ sq ft campus integrating engineering, production, and test", "Certified to ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, AS9100D, ITAR-registered", "Custom modular high-voltage battery systems with advanced lithium-ion chemistry", "Mobile power distribution systems with real-time monitoring and safety features"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1995 in Hanahan, SC by Rebecca and Phil Ufkes -> /about", "Woman-owned small business in South Carolina -> /about", "Campus spans more than 64,000 square feet -> /about", "Subsidiary of Albion River LLC (2025) -> /about", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, AS9100D -> /about, /quality", "ITAR-Registered -> /quality", "Industries: defense, aerospace, medical, industrial -> /about", "Products: mobile power distribution, battery systems, cable assemblies, etc. -> /, /about", "Capabilities: engineering design, manufacturing, testing, supply chain, program management, quality -> /, /about", "History: 2008 DoD mentoring with Raytheon, 2014 Arotech acquisition, 2019 Greenbriar, 2025 Albion River -> /about", "Quality standards: IPC-A-610 Class 1/2/3, IPC-J-STD-001, MIL-STD-810, etc. -> /quality", "RoHS-compliant production lines -> /quality", "Materials: advanced lithium-ion and other chemistries -> /about (Battery Systems section)", "Headquarters: Hanahan, South Carolina -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "UEC Advanced Electronics is a full-service product design and manufacturing company dedicated to delivering high-performance solutions for power products.", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR-Registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='uec-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='UMEC USA Inc. was established in 1984 in North Las Vegas, Nevada, as the United States design and sales office for the Taiwanese-owned Universal Microelectronics Corporation. The parent company, founded in Taiwan, has built a global presence in magnetic components, and the U.S. entity was created to support North American customers with local engineering and sales support.

The office focuses on magnetics for the DSL and broader telecommunications markets, offering services that range from simple coil winding to critical transformer design and manufacturing. Its product portfolio spans audio transformers, RF transformers, standard product lines, and custom designs, along with power electronics and magnetic components. UMEC USA leverages the parent corporation’s global manufacturing capabilities, with service branches across Asia, Europe, and North America, to deliver both off-the-shelf and tailored solutions.

The company’s expertise in transformer design for high-frequency and audio applications makes it a go-to source for telecom equipment builders and power supply designers.

