UPDATE companies SET description='Ultralife Corporation is headquartered in Newark, New York, where it operates a 280,000-square-foot manufacturing and office facility. The company is publicly traded on NASDAQ under the ticker ULBI. While its exact founding year is not disclosed in public materials, Ultralife has grown through strategic acquisitions, integrating brands such as Accutronics, Electrochem Solutions, Excell Battery, and Southwest Electronic Energy Group into a single global operation.

The company designs and manufactures lithium-based batteries, battery packs, chargers, and RF power systems for mission-critical applications. Its production capabilities span high-volume lithium-ion and thionyl chloride cell manufacturing at sites in Newark, Raynham (Massachusetts), and Shenzhen (China), as well as low- to high-volume pack assembly in Houston, the UK, Canada, and India. Ultralife offers more than 350 standard products and provides custom engineering, ruggedization, and lifecycle support lasting 10–15 years in the field.

Ultralife serves government and defense agencies, medical OEMs, industrial and oil-and-gas operators, and commercial customers. Its systems power ruggedized edge servers for Hewlett Packard Enterprise, hot-swappable medical cart batteries, downhole drilling monitors, autonomous underwater vehicles, surgical robots, and measurement-while-drilling tools. The customer base includes hundreds of global OEMs and defense contractors.

Ultralife differentiates itself by focusing on applications where commodity solutions fail, offering deep technical integration with customer design teams, a global footprint with manufacturing redundancy, and ISO 9001 and ISO 13485 certified quality systems. Financial stability as a NASDAQ-listed company and a transparent new-product-development workflow further support its position as a Tier 1 supplier.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','ISO 14001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Lithium-ion cell production", "Thionyl chloride cell production", "Battery pack assembly (low and high volume)", "Charger production", "Custom battery design and engineering", "RF power amplifier design and manufacturing", "Ruggedization of commercial electronics for harsh environments", "Systems integration for communications and compute", "New product development (NPD) and applications engineering", "Quality management (ISO 9001, ISO 13485)", "Supply chain management and scaling", "Regulatory and product documentation support", "Lifecycle support (10-15+ years)", "Cost-down exercises and design optimization", "Prototype to production scaling"], "industries": ["Government & Defense", "Medical", "Industrial", "Oil & Gas", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Lithium", "Lithium-ion", "Nickel-cadmium (NiCd)", "Thionyl chloride"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low to high volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineering teams operate where commodity solutions fail", "Strategic lifecycle support from concept through 10\u201315+ years in the field", "Global manufacturing footprint with facilities in North America, Europe, and Asia", "ISO 9001 and ISO 13485 certified quality management systems", "Manufacturing redundancy and risk management across multiple sites"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Newark, NY -> /about-us", "Publicly traded on NASDAQ (ULBI) -> /", "Acquisitions of Accutronics, Electrochem Solutions, Excell Battery, Southwest Electronic Ene