UPDATE companies SET description='United Semiconductors LLC was founded in 2005 in Los Alamitos, California. The company operates as a producer and supplier of binary and ternary III‑V semiconductor substrates.

The company specializes in bulk crystal growth of III‑V compounds, delivering polished, double‑sided wafers with diameters from 25 mm to 150 mm (1–6 in) and thicknesses of 0.5–10 mm. Its services span proprietary crystal growth, damage‑free wafer slicing and dicing (up to 75 mm), chemical‑mechanical grinding and polishing, high‑temperature impurity diffusion, activation and annealing (up to 1800 °C), and wet chemical etching, cleaning and passivation. It also produces research‑scale custom materials, nano‑inks (10–500 nm nanocrystals), luminescent powders, and optical components such as prisms and cubes.

United Semiconductors serves the microelectronics, optoelectronics, AI, space, and research sectors. Customers include researchers requiring small‑quantity custom synthesis, foundry partners for the company’s Optoelectronic AI Semiconductor Integrated Solutions (OASIS) Foundry, and organizations seeking space‑grown semiconductor crystals for radiation‑hardened devices.

The company emphasizes its proprietary crystal growth method, which yields uniform composition and high optical transmission with low defect density. It also highlights microgravity‑grown crystals for defect engineering and radiation hardening, and a damage‑free slicing process for both fragile and extremely hard materials.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Bulk crystal growth (ternary and binary III-V)", "Wafer slicing and dicing (up to 75 mm)", "Wafer grinding and chemical-mechanical polishing (up to 75 mm)", "Impurity diffusion, activation, and annealing (up to 1800\u00b0C)", "Wet chemical etching, cleaning, and passivation", "Research sample synthesis (custom materials)", "Nano-ink preparation (10\u2013500 nm nanocrystals)", "Luminescent powder synthesis", "Optical component fabrication (prisms, polygons, cubes)", "Space reagents for microelectronics fabrication", "OASIS Foundry partnership (optoelectronic AI semiconductor integrated solutions)"], "industries": ["Microelectronics", "Optoelectronics", "Artificial intelligence (AI)", "Space", "Research and development", "Semiconductor fabrication"], "materials": ["GaInAs", "GaInSb", "GaInP", "InAsP", "GaSb", "InAs", "InSb", "AlGaSb", "AlInSb", "CdS", "CdSe", "CdTe", "ZnO", "ZnS", "ZnSe", "ZnTe", "ZnCdS", "ZnCdTe", "ZnCdSe", "ZnCdO", "Ga2O3", "In2O3", "TiO2", "YAG:Ce", "KNbO3", "GaS", "GaSe", "GaSeS", "GaTe", "GaErAs", "GaErSb", "SiGe", "Rare-earth doped glasses", "Silicates", "Garnets", "Thiogallates", "Oxides", "Oxy-sulfides", "Sulfides", "Selenides"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary crystal growth method for uniform composition and high optical transmission", "Microgravity-grown semiconductor crystals enabling defect engineering and radiation hardening", "Damage-free wafer slicing and dicing for fragile and hard materials up to 75\u202fmm", "Custom wet chemical etching, cleaning, and passivation recipes developed per material", "High-temperature diffusion, activation, and annealing up to 1800\u202f\u00b0C in controlled atmospheres"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2005 -> db", "Headquarters Los Alamitos, California -> db", "Produces binary and ternary III-V semiconductors -> /", "Bulk crystal growth of ternary and binary III-V compounds, wafers 25-150 mm -> /about", "Services: crystal growth, wafer slicing/dicing, grinding/polishing, diffusion/annealing, wet etching/cleaning -> /services", "Materials: GaInAs, GaInSb, GaInP, InAsP, GaSb, InAs, InSb, AlGaSb, AlInSb, CdS, CdSe, CdTe, etc. -> /services", "Nano-inks with nanocrystals 10-500 nm -> /services", "Luminescent powders: silicates, garnets, thiogallates, oxides, oxy-sulfides, sulfides, selenides -> /services", "Space reagents for microelectronics fabrication -> /, /services", "OASIS Foundry for optoelectronic AI semiconductor integrated solutions -> /", "Proprietary crystal growth method for uniform composition and high optical transmission -> /services", "Microgravity-grown crystals for defect engineering and radiation hardening -> /", "Damage-free slicing for fragile and hard materials -> /services", "High-temperature annealing up to 1800\u00b0C -> /services", "Custom wet chemical etching recipes -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Producer and supplier of binary and ternary III-V semiconductors since 2005.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='united-semiconductors-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='UnityPoint at Home operates a home medical equipment storefront Suite 107 in Des Moines, Iowa.

The Des Moines location functions as a retail and rental center for home medical equipment. Its offerings span respiratory therapy — including home oxygen, CPAP and BiPAP devices, and a PAP resupply program — as well as maternity and nursing supplies such as Medela and Spectra breast pumps, nursing bras, and maternity support belts. The store also stocks a range of durable medical equipment: canes, walkers, crutches, bathroom safety aids, blood pressure monitors, compression stockings, incontinence products, phototherapy units, rollators, transport chairs, TENS units, and over-the-counter orthotics. Staff assist customers with equipment selection, fitting, and ongoing service and maintenance.

The store serves patients recovering at home, individuals with chronic respiratory conditions, and new or expecting mothers. It accepts all Medicare and Medicaid patients, making it a key access point for beneficiaries seeking covered durable medical equipment.

UnityPoint at Home emphasizes the convenience of physical storefronts where patients can try equipment before renting or purchasing. The company highlights its experienced staff who guide customers through options and address questions, aiming to simplify the process of obtaining and maintaining home medical equipment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Respiratory therapy", "Home oxygen therapy", "BiLevel Positive Airway Pressure (BiPAP)", "Continuous Positive Airway Pressure (CPAP)", "PAP resupply program", "Maternity and nursing support", "Medela breast pumps and supplies", "Spectra breast pumps and supplies", "Nursing bras and maternity support belts", "Canes, walkers, crutches and accessories", "Bathroom safety aids and products", "Blood pressure monitors", "Compression stockings", "Incontinence products and commodes", "Phototherapy", "Rollators and transport chairs", "Aids to daily living", "TENS units", "Over-the-counter orthotics", "Home medical equipment rental", "Home medical equipment sales", "Equipment service and maintenance"], "industries": ["Home Medical Equipment", "Durable Medical Equipment", "Respiratory Therapy", "Maternity and Nursing Care", "Home Medical Equipment Retail"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Storefront locations where patients can try equipment before renting or purchasing", "Experienced staff available to guide equipment selection and answer questions", "Accepts all Medicare and Medicaid patients for covered durable medical equipment", "PAP resupply program for ongoing CPAP/BiPAP supply needs", "Service and maintenance support for rented and purchased equipment"], "facts_used": ["Location: 1212 Pleasant Street, Suite 107, Des Moines, IA 50309 -> /", "Phone:  -> /", "Hours: Mon-Fri 8:30 AM - 4:30 PM -> /", "Services: Respiratory therapy, home oxygen, CPAP, BiPAP, PAP resupply, maternity/nursing supplies, DME products -> /", "Accept