-communications-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Utah Rustic Furniture by Bradley''s operates a 10,000-square-foot showroom at 2255 S 300 W in Salt Lake City, Utah. The business traces its roots to 1953, when Ralph Bradley opened his first furniture store in downtown Salt Lake City under the Bradley-Badger Furniture name. The company remains family-owned; after several transitions, Chad and Lesa Downs became sole owners in 1997, and their son Matt has managed the operation for two decades. The store describes itself as a third-generation family enterprise.

The retailer specializes in rustic and log furniture, much of it built by hand and made custom-to-order to customer specifications. Offerings include solid-wood bedroom sets, dining tables, accent pieces, and customizable American-made leather and fabric upholstery collections. A dedicated mattress department carries what the company calls Utah''s largest inventory of 100% natural and organic mattresses. The showroom also stocks lines from manufacturers such as Vaughn-Bassett, Benchcraft, Homelegance, Coaster, and Fashion Bed Group.

The company also serves shoppers seeking natural and organic sleep products.

