ollections.", "founded_year": "1953", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://g.page/r/CQQ2p54xAoREEBE/review"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='utah-rustic-furniture-by-bradley-s' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VR Industries, Inc. was founded in 1985 in Warwick, Rhode Island. The company has operated as an electronic contract manufacturer for nearly four decades, building a legacy of producing printed circuit board assemblies and electromechanical systems for a range of regulated industries.

The firm provides full-service manufacturing that spans printed circuit board assembly, electromechanical box-build integration, new product introduction, supply chain management, and program management. Its quality infrastructure includes automated optical inspection, high-resolution X-ray inspection, macro-zoom video inspection, and a counterfeit component verification program. All operators are certified to IPC-A-610 and J-STD-001 standards, and the facility maintains a Zero Defect program designed to reduce inspection time and cost.

VR Industries serves medical device OEMs, industrial equipment makers, U.S. military branches, green energy developers, and blue economy ventures. Medical customers include top global OEMs receiving moderate to complex PCBAs and full system assemblies. Defense work extends to every branch of the armed forces, supported by a workforce that includes veterans. Industrial clients receive custom electronic and mechanical assemblies built to ISO 9001, ISO 13485, FDA, and MIL-spec requirements.

The company emphasizes a partnership-driven model that prioritizes close collaboration from concept through delivery. Its differentiators include in-house IPC-certified trainers, a franchised-distributor supply chain strategy, and certifications covering ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ITAR, UL 508A, FDA registration, RoHS, and GIDEP.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','J-STD-001 (Space Addendum)','J-STD-001 CIT','J-STD-001 CIS','IPC-A-610','ITAR Registered','UL 508A','FDA Registered','RoHS Compliant','GIDEP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA)", "Electromechanical Assembly / Box Build", "New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Supply Chain Management", "Program Management", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "High-Resolution X-Ray Inspection", "Counterfeit Component Verification", "Burn-in Testing (component, product, system)", "J-STD-001 Certified Manufacturing", "IPC-A-610 Certified Inspection", "UL 508A Panel Building", "Medical Device Manufacturing (ISO 13485, FDA registered)", "Defense/ITAR Manufacturing", "RoHS Compliant Manufacturing", "Green Energy Manufacturing", "Blue Economy Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Medical", "Industrial", "Military", "Green Energy", "Blue Economy"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Automated Optical Inspection (AOI) Systems", "High-Resolution X-Ray Inspection", "Macro-zoom Video Inspection", "SMT Placement Machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Partnership-driven customer collaboration from concept to delivery", "Comprehensive quality certifications (ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ITAR, J-STD-001)", "Zero Defect program reducing inspection times and costs", "In-house IPC-certified trainers and specialists", "Counterfeit component verification with high-resolution X-ray", "Supply chain management sourcing from franchised distributors"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1985 -> /", "Headquarters Warwick, Rhode Island -> db", "ISO 9001 certified -> /quality", "ISO 13485 certified -> /quality", "ITAR registered -> /quality", "J-STD-001 certified -> /quality", "UL 508A -> /quality", "FDA registered -> /quality", "RoHS compliant -> /quality", "GIDEP -> /quality", "Industries: Medical, Industrial, Military, Green Energy, Blue Economy -> /", "Capabilities: PCBA, box build, NPI, supply chain, program management -> /", "Inspection: AOI, X-ray, macro-zoom video -> /quality", "Counterfeit component verification -> /quality", "Zero Defect program -> /quality", "Partnership-driven approach -> /", "Customer testimonials from Seven Consulting, Seven Media -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "VR Industries provides comprehensive electronic contract manufacturing solutions, focusing on Printed Circuit Board Assemblies (PCBA) and electromechanical assemblies (box builds).", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/vr-industries/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vr-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VSL Packaging operates from a design office and showroom at 239 West 29th Street in Manhattan''s Garment District. The company began in 2009 as the packaging arm of Varick Street Litho (VSL Print), a Manhattan commercial printer that has appeared on CNBC''s The Profit. VSL Packaging launched its own dedicated website in 2020, but the operation shares the West 29th Street address and the print craft heritage of its parent company.

The company designs, prototypes, and manufactures custom packaging — rigid boxes, folding cartons, corrugated boxes, retail bags, point-of-purchase displays, corrugated shippers, and luxury mailers — all produced in New York City. The process moves through structural design, photorealistic 3D rendering, physical prototyping, dieline creation, and pre-production proofs before printing and finishing. Finishing options include embossing, debossing, foil stamping, spot UV, matte, gloss, satin, and soft-touch lamination. VSL also provides shipping and fulfillment services such as kitting, assembly, warehousing, pick-pack-ship, and freight coordination. The company reports more than 10,000 packaging projects completed across 16 box styles.

VSL serves roughly two dozen industries, including apparel, beauty, beverages, CBD, cosmetics, electronics, food, jewelry, luxury goods, medical, pharmaceuticals, and sporting goods. Its customer base ranges from early-stage startups to national brands; documented projects include packaging for Belvedere Vodka, Google, IBM, Betty Booze, Bored Cow, and Charlie Fox.

VSL differentiates itself by controlling the entire production chain under one roof: the design desk, prototyping bench, press schedule, and finishing work all reside at the same Manhattan address. The company emphasizes that it owns the job it sells, avoiding brokers and overseas factories. Quote follow-up occurs within one business day, and minimum order quantities are kept low and flexible, quoted per project.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural design", "3D rendering", "Physical prototyping", "Dieline creation", "Pre-production proofs", "Custom rigid box manufacturing", "Folding carton manufacturing", "Corrugated box manufacturing", "Retail bag manufacturing", "POP display manufacturing", "Corrugated shipper manufacturing", "Luxury mailer manufacturing", "Embossing", "Debossing", "Foil stamping", "Spot UV coating", "Matte coating", "Gloss coating", "Satin coating", "Soft-touch lamination", "Kitting and assembly", "Warehousing", "Pick-pack-ship", "Freight coordination"], "industries": ["apparel", "beauty", "beverages", "CBD", "commercial", "cosmetics", "ecommerce", "electronics", "food", "footwear", "gift", "health", "home goods", "industrial", "jewelry", "luxury", "medical", "nutraceuticals", "pet care", "pharmaceuticals", "retail", "sporting goods"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Design, prototype, and production all under one roof in Manhattan", "Quote follow-up within one business day", "Low, flexible minimum order quantities with no fixed public minimum", "3D renderings, physical prototypes, and pre-production proofs before any run", "Print craft heritage from Varick Street Litho (VSL Print)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 as packaging arm of Varick Street Litho -> db, homepage", "Design office and showroom at 239 West 29th Street, Manhattan -> homepage, about", "Produces custom boxes, bags, mailers, POP displays, shippers -> homepage", "Offers structural 